# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/next-1 windows (the ship-5 candidate; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next-1 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt, ORDER-W2.txt and
# ORDER-SHIP.txt have the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules of the three runs.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (sed -i 's/tp4-next-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file
# the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C2_MODEL_REPO / C2_MODEL_REVISION (qwen_c2_checkpoint.py): a job that carries them serves the Swift checkpoint (what production serves) from its own converted-weight directory and, since NP9, with the output
# ceiling of its catalog entry; the keys are the same in every smoke and prefix job of this pack (the prefix gate serves the selection in its containers too and fails an arm whose log lacks the checkpoint lines), so each pair
# differs by the profile alone. The replay and build steps do not forward the selection (the job reader refuses the keys beside them): they run the base checkpoint.
# T1A (TIMED, the CONTROL of the pair): the approved ship-4 profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s4 on Swift, the stack production runs: a lone
# live user decodes on the 4-row per-request engine, two or three on the padded 64-row block, four on the full block, six or more on the octo block. Tests: np1_live1,
# np1_live2 and np1_live4 (one, two and four users started together on about 3,500-token real-code prompts, every answer to EXACTLY 2,000 tokens with ignore_eos, so the
# all-live window is long enough to read at either rate) and concurrent8_steady (eight users: the octo block, which the lone-user round never touches, so a parity row and
# the boot-to-boot floor), then agent_turns (production-shaped traffic). AGENT TURNS (agent_turns.py, tp4/agent-turns): SIX sessions of 64k, 128k and 200k tokens of coding
# context, each a cold opening request and then 12 returning turns (a ~150-400 token tool result appended after the previous answer verbatim, 200-600 tokens out, a 1-8 s
# tool gap), every session under its own cache_salt (the smoke step writes a throwaway salt key and mounts it only for this test). It is the one smoke that reaches the
# prefix store, sticky sessions, the engine rebind, exact resume (the undrop and the carry) and the lone-user round at the live counts a real conversation mix produces. A
# MEASUREMENT, no speed threshold: the judge fails an errored or timed-out request, a request with no tokens or no finish, and a salted run that reuses nothing on more than
# 10% of its returning turns. The six contexts total about 800,000 tokens of the 1,055,488-token pool, so it does not force the host tier (A3 does). `python3
# scripts/ci/agent_turns.py report --smoke-log <smoke> --container-log <container>` prints the rates, the TTFT by context bucket, the re-prefilled tokens and the per-live
# table; run it on both legs of the pair and set them side by side.. Every boot a fresh reset. RUN WITH THE CI PAUSED: the ARC runner sets are at ZERO for this job (ORDER,
# ARC-ZERO); no build, no CI push, no other job beside it. CHECKPOINT READ (the workflow passes c2_smoke_check.py --expect-checkpoint): the container log holds "[QWEN-C2]
# checkpoint ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b@b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4 key=... weight_cache=.../weights-ckpt/<key> base_cache=... (the base cache is not read or
# written)" once, a "weight cache ...: found" line (the cache the Swift window built; this pack never builds it) and the worker's "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint bound ..." line; the
# models answer names ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b. TELEMETRY (C2_TELEMETRY=1, scripts/ci/card_telemetry.py): the read-only ARC sidecar samples every chip once a second
# through the smoke step; the first [TELEMETRY] line must say decode check ok. A rate difference that comes with a different loaded AICLK between the arms is the clocks,
# not the lever. Duration (estimate): 45 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s4
C2_MODEL_REPO=ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b
C2_MODEL_REVISION=b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,np1_live1,np1_live2,np1_live4,concurrent8_steady,agent_turns
C2_TELEMETRY=1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=95
